data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** The test compiled and ran successfully on .NET 11 (preview). Here's what works:

```csharp
Span<nint>  a = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> b = stackalloc nuint[2];
```

Output confirmed correct values including `nint.MaxValue` (9223372036854775807 on this 64-bit system) and `nuint.MaxValue` (18446744073709551615). Native-sized integers (`nint`/`nuint`, introduced in C# 9) are valid `stackalloc` element types just like any other unmanaged type.
